{
  "id": "wc5e-bestiary",
  "title": "Warcraft 5e (WC5E) — moved to a new module",
  "description": "<p><strong>This module has moved and is no longer updated here.</strong> It is now published by the WC5E project as <strong>wc5e-foundryvtt</strong>.</p><p><strong>To move across:</strong> install the new module from <a href=\"https://github.com/WC5E/wc5e-foundryvtt\">its repository</a>, using the manifest URL on that page — <code>https://github.com/WC5E/wc5e-foundryvtt/releases/latest/download/module.json</code> — then disable and uninstall this one. If that URL does not resolve yet, the new module's first release is still being cut; check the repository. Nothing is lost meanwhile — this module keeps working exactly as it does now.</p><p>Foundry treats the new module as a separate install, so there is no automatic upgrade. Compendium content is the same. Anything you already dragged into a world came from <em>this</em> module and keeps working, but re-drag it from the new compendiums so it stays linked to the module that is still maintained.</p><p>Content is unchanged from v1.18.3; this release exists only to tell you where the module went. <a href=\"https://github.com/WC5E/wc5e-foundryvtt\">New repository</a>.</p>",
